// FIX-S51 (v13.0 — SINGLE-SESSION IDENTITY CONVERGENCE):
//   Root cause (verified across 6 scan cycles):
//     `resolveSocketVisitorId` produced yet another visitorId
//     format (`visitorId || 'ip_'+ip || 'tc_'+tc`), which did NOT
//     collide with data.js (`visitorId || 'tc_'+tc`), redirect.js
//     (`visitorId || bare-ip`), or webhook.js
//     (`visitorId || 'ip_'+ip || 'tc_'+tc`). One visitor =
//     4 different visitorId strings = 4 different sessions.
//     Additionally `emitSessionDelta` (socket-init path) emitted
//     ONLY to `room_<ownerCode>`, so a socket that had joined
//     `room_<trackingCode>` via `joinRoom(trackingCode)` never
//     received the delta. And `disconnect`'s Offline flip emitted
//     a sessionDelta WITHOUT `visitorId`, so the client hD merge
//     preserved a stale visitorId.
//
//   FIX:
//     1. `resolveSocketVisitorId` delegates to the canonical
//        `identity.normalizeVisitorId` helper (same as data.js /
//        redirect.js / webhook.js).
//     2. `emitSessionDelta` now emits to BOTH `room_<ownerCode>`
//        AND `room_<trackingCode>` (parity with webhook.js).
//     3. `disconnect`'s Offline-flip payload now includes
//        `visitorId` so client merges stay consistent.
//   No other behaviour, route, CORS, rate-limit, session-manager,
//   or 24h-cycle contract changed.
// ============================================================

